course: dictionary
lesson: 1202
title: Context clues: buckle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, so the words around it tell you which one is right. Buckle can be a noun or a verb. A buckle is a clip that fastens two ends together, like on a belt. To buckle is to fasten with one.
explain: «A helmet fits snug and level, just above the eyebrows, with the strap buckled; a loose helmet does not protect.» A loose helmet does not protect you, so buckled must mean fastened tight. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Bridges grow a little in summer and shrink in winter, and the gaps with metal teeth stop them cracking or buckling.» Here buckling is not about clips at all. The bridge is bending or crumpling under the heat, so buckle can also mean bend or give way. The word that matters is the context: the heat and the bridge.
explain: Buckle changes meaning again in «If your knees buckle, they suddenly bend.» The clue is that you are weak or scared. Buckle down and buckle under are informal phrases, so their meanings do not come from the single word alone: buckle down means start working hard, and buckle under means give in.
fact: A buckle is a metal or plastic clip that fastens two ends together, on a belt, strap or shoe.
fact: «Buckle up» means fasten your seat belt every time you are in a car.
fact: To buckle can mean to bend, crumple or collapse under weight or heat, like a bridge or a railway track in summer.
fact: If your knees buckle, they suddenly bend because you are weak or scared.
fact: «Buckle down» means start working hard, and «buckle under» means give in.
exercise: «Buckle your seat belt.» What does buckle mean here? | Hide | Bend | *Fasten | Shout
exercise: «The gaps with metal teeth stop bridges cracking or buckling.» What does buckling mean here? | *Bending or crumpling under heat | Painting with bright colours | Growing taller in winter | Ringing like a bell
exercise: Lily says her knees buckle when she sees the big dog. What does buckle mean? | Run very fast | Get bigger and taller | *Suddenly bend because she is scared | Start to sing
test: Aisha says, «Please buckle your helmet before you ride.» What does buckle mean here? | Shake | Paint | Lose | *Fasten
test: Tom must buckle down to finish his project. What does buckle down mean? | Lose his bag | *Start working hard | Give in to the teacher | Lie down and rest
exam: «A loose helmet does not protect.» What should you do with a bike helmet's strap? | *Buckle it so the helmet sits snug and level | Tie it in a knot | Wear the helmet at the back of your head | Leave it loose so it feels comfortable
